🚽 Regression for #376: yapping/baka/yapto format parser must not read past
🚽 end of buffer on a bare/incomplete % specifier. Previously the flag-skipping
🚽 loop used strchr(set, *format) without a NUL guard, and strchr(set, '\0')
🚽 returns non-NULL (the set's own terminator), so a format ending with "%",
🚽 "%5", "%.*", "%l", "%h", "%j" etc walked off the end and read OOB.
🚽 Fixed by guarding the loop with *format && and guarding the length-modifier
🚽 check similarly. Each yapping below ends with an incomplete specifier and
🚽 must not crash, not emit garbage, and must still flush the literal prefix
🚽 deterministically (the incomplete conversion is dropped, prefix is kept).
skibidi main {
    yapping("A%", 1);
    yapping("B%5", 2);
    yapping("C%.*", 3);
    yapping("D%l", 4);
    yapping("E%h", 5);
    yapping("F%j", 6);
    yapping("G%#", 7);
    yapping("ok");
    bussin 0;
}
